Reading: no formalizer failure becomes a wrong output; each becomes an abstention whose final search must scan the whole run, n = 2 n0 distinct task queries with caching (about 8n0/3 without). These searches exceed Theorem 5(d)'s 2n0 - 1, as its (A2) clause allows. The cost grows with the number of problems, not with K.

## Part 4. Effort arithmetic

Worst case, search queries only, V-machine, beta = 0: VSI 2 n0 K. Bar: a fifth of chained imitation's 20 n0 K, i.e. 4 n0 K. Abstentions at rate phi, each costing c n0 task queries. Bar: 2K + c phi T <= 4K, so T <= 2K/(c phi). Human-does-it baseline (n0 T): T > 2K/(1 - c phi). A window exists iff phi < 1/(2c).

| phi | c = 2 (cached scan): T_max/K | baseline T_min/K | c = 8/3 (uncached): T_max/K | T_min/K | c = 3 (cached, then the human does it): T_max/K | T_min/K |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0.05 | 20.0 | 2.2 | 15.0 | 2.3 | 13.3 | 2.4 |
| 0.1 | 10.0 | 2.5 | 7.5 | 2.7 | 6.7 | 2.9 |
| 0.2 | 5.0 | 3.3 | 3.8 | 4.3 (no window) | 3.3 | 5.0 (no window) |
| 0.3 | 3.3 | 5.0 (no window) | 2.5 | 10.0 (no window) | 2.2 | 20.0 (no window) |

